<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Two draws without replacement</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]A box holds \({@r@}\) blue pens and \({@b@}\) red pens.[[else]]A basket at a market in Mombasa holds \({@r@}\) ripe mangoes and \({@b@}\) unripe mangoes.[[/if]] Two [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]pens[[else]]mangoes[[/if]] are taken at random, one after the other, without replacement.</p><p>Give each probability exactly, as a fraction or an exact decimal.</p><p>(a) The first [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]pen[[else]]mango[[/if]] is [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]. What is the probability that the second is [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]?</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the probability that both are [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) Find the probability that one is [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]] and one is [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div><p>(d) Find the probability that at least one is [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]].</p><div>[[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]] [[feedback:prt4]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Without replacement, count what is left at the second stage: one [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]pen[[else]]mango[[/if]] has gone, so there are \({@n-1@}\) left. The four paths of the tree are</p><table border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><tr><th style="padding:4px 10px;">First</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Second</th><th style="padding:4px 10px;">Probability of the path</th></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\dfrac{{@r@}}{{@n@}} \times \dfrac{{@r-1@}}{{@n-1@}} = {@r*(r-1)/(n*(n-1))@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\dfrac{{@r@}}{{@n@}} \times \dfrac{{@b@}}{{@n-1@}} = {@r*b/(n*(n-1))@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\dfrac{{@b@}}{{@n@}} \times \dfrac{{@r@}}{{@n-1@}} = {@r*b/(n*(n-1))@}\)</td></tr><tr><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">[[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]]</td><td style="padding:4px 10px;">\(\dfrac{{@b@}}{{@n@}} \times \dfrac{{@b-1@}}{{@n-1@}} = {@b*(b-1)/(n*(n-1))@}\)</td></tr></table><p>(a) After a [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]] [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]pen[[else]]mango[[/if]] is taken, \({@r-1@}\) of the \({@n-1@}\) left are [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]: \({@ta1@}\).</p><p>(b) \(\dfrac{{@r@}}{{@n@}} \times \dfrac{{@r-1@}}{{@n-1@}} = {@ta2@}\).</p><p>(c) Two paths: [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]] then [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]], or [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]] then [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]. \({@r*b/(n*(n-1))@} + {@r*b/(n*(n-1))@} = {@ta3@}\).</p><p>(d) <q>At least one [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]red[[else]]unripe[[/if]]</q> is everything except both [[if test="is(cx=1)"]]blue[[else]]ripe[[/if]]: \(1 - {@ta2@} = {@ta4@}\). The four paths add to 1.</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
