  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Probability III: two draws without replacement</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Essential 3.2: Find second-stage probabilities by counting what is left, and use a two-stage tree without replacement for both, one of each and at least one.</p><p id="edition">Essential</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 3, Section E, question E2 of Cassell, D., Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P. and Shilton, S., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Statistics 1 for Edexcel, Cambridge University Press, 2004: pens and mangoes in new numbers, randomised, with an 'at least one' part.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Essential Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
